atlas surface

architecture schema-workspace
  canonical_name Schema workspace
  family surface
  domain Surface / Database structure and migration
  layer application
  semantic_question For a SQLite database, which structural changes are wanted, which rows would each change reject, alter or orphan, and does the resulting migration keep every row and reference when run on a copy?
  purpose A Work Samples workspace from the claude-skills engineering schema donors as an instrument: a SQLite file opened in the browser with sql.js, drawn as tables with their references, changes staged from the drawing and the column editor, each change checked against the data, a migration written by SQLite's documented table-rebuild procedure, and a trial on a copy reporting rows before and after, broken references and the integrity check; the original is never written and the result is a download
  maturity implemented
  consumes sql.js 1.12.0 (SQLite compiled to WebAssembly), vendored with npm integrity and SHA-256 in vendor/sql.js-1.12.0/provenance.tsv
  publishes migration SQL, changed SQLite file, diagram SVG
  node_types Table, Column, ForeignKey, Index, StagedChange, Precheck, Trial
  internal_calculus changes ALTER TABLE cannot make rebuild the table: create T__new, copy with casts and fills, drop, rename, recreate indexes, then PRAGMA foreign_key_check, all with foreign keys off inside one transaction
  internal_calculus renaming a table or a referred-to column also rebuilds every table whose definition names it
  invariant CHECK clauses written in a table survive a rebuild, as do composite keys, table-level UNIQUE, AUTOINCREMENT and WITHOUT ROWID
  invariant a required column over empty values needs a fill; a reference needs a single-column key or unique target; a value retyped is shown with what it becomes before running
  invariant a failed trial rolls back and names the statement that failed; the copy is discarded
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/schema-lab.test.mjs with bun:sqlite over the sample built from retained research and NYC 311 records: references hold in the sample, retyping years keeps every row and the precheck names "c. 1999" becoming 0, renaming people/id rebuilds authorship and its reference still holds, an orphan reference is found before and listed after, a required column takes its fill, a unique index over duplicates fails on the copy leaving it unchanged, a CHECK survives a rebuild, and impossible changes are refused with reasons
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/queues-research-browser.mjs in headless Chrome at 1440 and 390 px: works.year retyped from the column editor, tried on the copy, all six tables kept their rows and every reference held
  forbidden_inference a migration that passes on a copy -> one that is safe on a database other programs are writing to, or under another SQLite version
  forbidden_inference a structure change -> a correct data model for the business
  known_gap not yet published; the deploy is the operator's to run
  known_gap views, triggers and generated columns are listed by SQLite but not edited or rewritten by a rebuild
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/schema-lab.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/schema-lab-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/schema-lab-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/schema-lab.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/schema.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/vendor/sql.js-1.12.0/provenance.tsv
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/schema-lab.test.mjs
  source_lineage 2026-10-19 claude-skills engineering/* at 19392f7a; earlier ChatGPT build was sandbox-only

interaction service-site-packages-schema-workspace
  source service-site
  destination schema-workspace
  relation packages_workspace
  preserves a sample database built from the retained research and 311 records, and the vendored SQLite with its provenance
  drops nothing a visitor opens; their file stays in their browser
  forbidden_inference a packaged workspace -> a published one
  invalidates_on schema-lab sources, sql.js vendor files, retained records
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/schema-lab-material.mjs

architecture dependency-planner
  canonical_name Dependency planner
  family surface
  domain Surface / Plans, dependencies and finish dates
  layer application
  semantic_question For tasks with best, likely and worst lengths, who does them and what each waits on, which path decides the end, how likely is each finish date, and how much later does it end when one person can do one thing at a time?
  purpose A Work Samples workspace from the claude-skills project-management donors as an instrument: a timeline edited directly (drag a bar's end to change its length, drag its dot onto another task to make that task wait), the critical path from likely lengths, 3,000 seeded PERT-Beta runs giving finish-date percentiles and how often each task is critical, a serial schedule that respects each person's time, and a finish-date chart where dragging picks a date and shows its chance; the sample is this estate's own open handoff work read from the backfill ledger
  maturity implemented
  consumes docs/engineering/handoff-backfill-20261019/demo-instruments.tsv
  publishes schedule CSV, plan JSON
  node_types Task, Dependency, ThreePointEstimate, Owner, SimulatedFinish, LevelledSchedule
  internal_calculus forward and backward passes for early and late dates and slack; loops are found by depth-first search and refused
  internal_calculus PERT-Beta draws with shape 1 + 4(m - o)/(p - o) via Marsaglia–Tsang gamma variates
  internal_calculus levelling: at each step the ready task whose owner is free soonest starts, least slack first
  invariant a dependency that would close a loop is refused with the tasks named; estimates must run best ≤ likely ≤ worst
  invariant dates count working days and skip Saturdays and Sundays; the same seed gives the same spread
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/plan-network.test.mjs checks a textbook network's critical path, slack and late dates by hand, loop and missing-task refusal, PERT draw range and mean, a repeatable spread wider than the likely plan with the long path critical in more than 85% of runs, a two-day delay when one person holds two parallel tasks, working-day arithmetic over a weekend, and CSV round trips
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/queues-research-browser.mjs in headless Chrome at 1440 and 390 px: the sample scheduled at least ten tasks, simulated finish dates, showed the people view and refused a dependency loop
  forbidden_inference a percentile date -> a commitment or a forecast of what will happen; the spread comes from the stated estimates
  forbidden_inference the sample's estimates -> measured effort; they are labelled assumptions
  known_gap not yet published; the deploy is the operator's to run
  known_gap calendars without weekends only; holidays, part-time owners and partial overlaps are not modelled
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/plan-network.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/plan-network-client.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/plan-network-material.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/plan-network.css
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/sections/plan.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/plan-network.test.mjs
  source_lineage 2026-10-19 claude-skills project-management/* at 19392f7a; earlier ChatGPT build was sandbox-only

interaction dependency-planner-reads-handoff-ledger
  source dependency-planner
  destination service-site
  relation packages_workspace
  preserves the open rows of the instrument ledger as the sample's tasks
  drops the ledger's stage evidence; the plan carries titles and states only
  forbidden_inference the sample plan -> an agreed schedule
  invalidates_on demo-instruments.tsv
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/plan-network-material.mjs
